>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Del`

``` hol4
clasetLib.Del : string -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a named classical rule for removal during one tactic invocation.

`Del name` produces a theorem marker recognized in classical tactic theorem
lists. Before running the tactic, every rule with exactly that claset name
is removed from the temporary rule set. Stored theorem rules normally use a
fully qualified database name such as `bool$AND_INTRO_THM`. Removing an
absent name has no effect.

`Del` neither changes the current theory's classical rule set nor removes
the theorem from the theorem database. For persistent or session-local
programmatic removal, use `delrule` or `temp_delrule`. There is no classical
rule-removal theorem attribute. `Del` is distinct from the simplifier's
`Excl` marker.

### Failure

`Del name` does not fail. Processing the marker is also a no-op when `name`
is not present.

### Example

The seed conjunction-introduction rule is suppressed only in this call:

``` hol4
TRY (classicalLib.SAFE_TAC
       [clasetLib.Del "bool$AND_INTRO_THM"])
```

A later `SAFE_TAC []` again sees the seed rule.

